<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia's Dadas tumbles 13 pct on bankruptcy talk.</title>
<headline>Slovenia's Dadas tumbles 13 pct on bankruptcy talk.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Slovenian brokerage Dadas tumbled 13.50 percent in late-morning trade following a newspaper report that it may face bankruptcy if the merger with Primofin is not approved by its shareholders, traders said.</p>
<p>No-one at Dadas was available for comment.</p>
<p>The shareholders meeting is scheduled for November 29.</p>
<p>At 1154 GMT, Dadas was down 13.50 percent or 1,620 tolars at 10,380 tolars on volume of 515 shares.</p>
<p>Brokerage Primofin was down 6.45 percent or 2,000 tolars at 29,010 tolars on volume of 200 shares.</p>
<p>-- Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
</text>
